**R14: Strategy and overview questions can miss the key sentence** · Status: Open
T07 AMD and T45 Intel (answer in the MD&A overview) and T59 Netflix and T34 eBay (one sentence in Item 1) still miss after `intent`. The right filing is found; the sentence is not lifted into the top 5.

**R15: Cover-page fields can be lost** · Impact: Data · Status: Open
Carlisle FY2024: the cover chunk keeps "(State or other jurisdiction of incorporation)" but not the word "Delaware", so the state of incorporation cannot be answered from the index (T18).

**R16: Latest-year lookups for facts on table pages** · Status: Open
"Where is Xylem headquartered?" (no year) returns the 2021 properties page; the 2025 cover address is not ranked (T100).

**R17: Typo repair can change ranking** · Status: Known
`typo` replaces unknown words with close, frequent words (proft -> profit). It fixed 3 questions but also moved T17 (Carlisle segments, "busness" -> "business") from rank 4 to outside the top 5.

**R18: Roman Urdu support is a word list** · Status: Known
`roman` maps common words (banati, bechti, kab bani, nuqsan ...). Questions phrased mostly in Roman Urdu still depend on their English words (T55 Meta still misses); the embedding model is English-only.

**R19: Some chunks start mid-word** · Impact: Cosmetic, minor for keyword search · Status: Open
Example: "ct offerings in nine key categories" (Nike FY2017), most likely where a long text was split by characters. The first word of such a chunk is lost to keyword search.

**R20: Bullet items missing from chunks** · Impact: Data · Status: Open
`check_data.py --bullets`: 697 of 40,027 bullet items (1.7%) in the PDFs appear in no chunk. Cause: rescue passes 3 and 4 in `table_analyzer.py` take short list lines as table candidates, and `paragraph_parser.py` skips table lines. Planned: a bullet guard plus returning unused candidate lines to paragraphs.

### Retrieval stage: v2.4 and v2.4.1 (Nov 2026), then frozen

**R21: Section-title questions returned cross-references instead of the section** · Status: Resolved (v2.4)
Found by the supervisor in the 12 Nov demo: "Amazon 2022, page 26, Item 7" returned chunks that only mention Item 7 instead of the section's first page. v2.4 adds a `heading` feature (section title and Item number matched against a heading index). The 100-question test stayed at 90/100 with identical ranking.

**R22: Some operating-expense tables lose their numbers** · Impact: Data · Status: Open
The header "Amount | Amount" is kept but the values are dropped, for example Palo Alto Networks FY2025 R&D table (p. 52). The answer layer correctly reports the figure as not stated; for the 12 core metrics the SQL track supplies the value from SEC XBRL.

**R23: A year followed by a comma was ignored** · Status: Resolved (v2.4.1)
The year pattern rejected any year followed by a comma (to skip numbers such as 2,020,000), so "in 2020, Kennametal" and "in 2023, according to" lost their year filter. Found by the SQL test set (7 of 150 failures). It affected 2 of the 100 test questions (T57, T88) and 1 golden question; all three still rank the answer at #1. The 100-question test is unchanged at 90/100.

**Retrieval freeze (26 Nov 2026).** With top-20 results on the 100 questions: answer at #1 for 58, #2-5 for 32, #6-20 for 3 (T17, T42, T45), not in the top 20 for 7 (T07, T18, T34, T44, T55, T59, T100). The 7 misses are cover-page fields (R15, R16) and broad strategy or overview questions (R14). After five tuned versions, further changes would be fitted to the same 100 questions, so the retriever is frozen at v2.4.1 and its unbiased figure comes from the held-out set (section 9).

