## 8. SQL track (structured financial data)

**Layers.** Raw: every PDF table cell (1,004,264 facts). External: SEC XBRL company facts for all 50 companies (1,303,114 facts). Curated: 12 metrics per filing with cross-year and balance checks. Serving (`financials`): one final value per company, fiscal year and metric (5,389 values, 98.9% backed by SEC XBRL), the standard XBRL concept per metric, PDF page citation when the PDF value equals it, and the prior-year value from the same filing for restatement-aware changes.

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| PDF-extracted metrics vs SEC XBRL | 4,250 / 4,339 = 97.9% |
| Serving values checked by hand against the PDFs (60, weighted to risky groups) | 55/60 at audit; 59/60 after two fixes |
| Routing on a fresh held-out set (150 number questions) | 149/150 = 99.3% (95% CI 96.3-99.9) |
| Non-number questions given structured data by mistake | 0/50 |

Bugs found and fixed on the way: year followed by a comma (R23); one standard concept per metric (Kimberly-Clark net income incl. noncontrolling interest, Walmart net sales vs total revenue); next year's filing taken for a missing year (Dell FY2019); 52/53-week years ending in early January (Franklin Electric FY2015 read as 2016); changes computed across a restatement (Boeing 2017-2018 total assets, +27% vs +4.4%). The first test set (95.3%) was used to find the comma bug, so a fresh set (test2) gives the reported figure.

**F1: Operating income tagged on segment earnings** · Impact: Data · Status: Open
Rockwell Automation has no GAAP operating income line; its XBRL `OperatingIncomeLoss` is total segment operating earnings (FY2023: 1,929.8). The value is served as operating income. Company-specific; not fixed to avoid a one-off rule.

**F2: Fiscal-year label differs from the company's own name** · Status: Known
In the SQL track, fiscal year = the calendar year in which the period ends. Home Depot calls the year ending in January 2024 "fiscal 2023"; the SQL track labels it FY2024, while the PDF chunks follow the company's own label (S2), so the two tracks can differ by one year for Home Depot. A question using the company's own label can get a one-year-off structured value.

**F3: Revenue includes other income for some companies** · Status: By design
The standard concept `Revenues` is total revenues. For Chevron this includes income from equity affiliates and other income (FY2025: 189,031 vs sales and other operating revenues 184,432).

**F4: Per-share values across a stock split are not adjusted** · Status: Known
Each year's EPS is as originally reported. Chipotle's 50-for-1 split in 2024 makes FY2020 EPS (12.52) and FY2025 EPS (1.14) not comparable; the answer does not mention the split.

**F5: "cash from <year>" read as cash from operations** · Status: Open
"List WTS's cash from 2018 through 2021" got no structured data because "cash from" matches the operating-cash-flow phrase list (the one miss on test2).

**F6: Gaps** · Status: Known
Chevron FY2019 revenue has no value (absent from both the PDF curated layer and SEC data for that filing). 8 PDF-only values far from the company's SEC values are flagged `pdf_suspect` and never served.

