## 9. Answer layer (LLM)

**Setup.** Retriever top 5 (8 for comparisons) plus, for number questions, one structured source [D1]; GPT-OSS-120B on Groq (free tier) with Gemini and other Groq models as fallback; grounded prompt with citations; refusal when retrieval finds no matching company or year.

**Dev evaluation (100 questions, used for tuning; 95 run so far).**

| Measure | Result |
|---|---|
| LLM judge (Qwen3), correct | 84/95 = 88.4% |
| Human labels, correct | 88/95 = 92.6% |
| Judge-human agreement (correct / partial / wrong) | 86/95 = 90.5%, Cohen's kappa 0.46 (0.51 correct vs other) |
| Faithfulness, judge | 91/95 = 95.8% |
| Faithfulness, human | 87/95 = 91.6% |

The judge was calibrated blind (its verdicts hidden from the reviewer). It is stricter than the human on completeness (5 answers it called partial were complete for the question asked) and misses small unsupported additions (it found 2 of the 8 the human flagged). Low kappa with high agreement is expected when about 90% of answers fall in one class. Human-labelled faithfulness is reported.

**SQL source on vs off (27 Nov).** Same model, judge and prompt (v3) on the 99 dev questions that ran in both: correct 87 → 88, faithfulness 94 → 95; of the 12 questions that receive [D1], 10 → 11 correct (T84 fixed); none got worse. The SQL source is on by default.

**A1: Small unsupported additions** · Impact: Data · Status: Open (prompt v4 under test)
Examples: "damage reputation" added to a security-risk answer (T81), "partners could become competitors" (T29), "supply chain disruption" (T25), "licensed stores contribute the remainder" (T87). Prompt v4 adds rules against unstated effects and scope changes; default stays v3 until measured.

**A2: Scope widened** · Status: Open (prompt v4)
A segment's facilities presented as the whole company's (T91: Walmart International's 221 distribution facilities); a risk factor's "may pursue acquisitions" presented as strategy (T07).

**A3: Abbreviation expanded without a source** · Status: Open
"CWT" expanded as "Carlisle WeatherTech" (T17), although the prompt forbids invented expansions.

**A4: Citation on the wrong source** · Impact: Cosmetic · Status: Known
Correct content tagged with a neighbouring source (T47, T89). The claim exists in the retrieved set, but the tag points to a different chunk.

**A5: Charts are not read** · Status: By design
Numbers shown only in images (for example Meta's daily active users chart) are not in the text index.

**A6: Prompt larger than the free tier's per-minute limit** · Impact: Data · Status: Known (free tier only)
T96 (Woodward share repurchases) builds a prompt of about 9,000 tokens; Groq's free tier allows 8,000 tokens per minute on GPT-OSS-120B and 7,000 input tokens per minute on the Qwen3 judge. It can never run there, however long the wait. The answer layer reports it as `too_large` and the evaluation leaves it out of the percentages for every run, so comparisons stay on the same questions. The paid tier (250K tokens per minute) removes the limit.

**Pending:** prompt v4 on the dev set (65 of 100 answered so far); one run on 60 held-out questions written by hand from random 10-K pages (29 text, 21 number, 10 two-company comparisons; easy 17, medium 31, hard 12), with human labels.

